diff --git a/packages/client/ui-brand-qizhi/README.md b/packages/client/ui-brand-qizhi/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..02b9913c7b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/client/ui-brand-qizhi/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,158 @@
+---
+description: "启智AGENT brand occupants for the Web client's sidebar and conversation hero slots, replacing the official DeepSeek marks."
+kind: "package-reference"
+---
+
+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-brand-qizhi
+
+A deployment brand package that fills the generic browser-brand slots with the
+**启智AGENT** identity: the sidebar mark, the sidebar name, and the empty-session
+hero emblem with its ambient particle layer. It is the alternative-brand package
+that [`dsh-client-ui-brand-official`](../ui-brand-official/README.md) points to
+when it says a differently-branded deployment should supply its own package.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Use this package](#use-this-package)
+- [Understand the implementation](#understand-the-implementation)
+- [Model Experience](#model-experience)
+- [Known Limitations and Deferred Work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)
+
+-----
+
+<a id="use-this-package"></a>
+## Use this package
+
+Mount it in place of the official brand row. The web-app bundle does exactly
+that in `packages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml`:
+
+```yaml
+- id: ui-brand-qizhi
+  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-brand-qizhi'
+```
+
+Three slots change hands, and nothing else:
+
+| Slot | Owner surface | Shipped fallback | This package |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `sidebar.brand.mark` | `ui-sidebar` (`SidebarRoot.tsx`) | `FishLogo` | `QizhiBrandMark` — hexagonal core, four-point spark, three circuit nodes |
+| `sidebar.brand.name` | `ui-sidebar` | `brand.localBuild` text | `QizhiBrandName` — 启智 in a gradient, `AGENT` in tracked capitals |
+| `conversation.hero.brand.mark` | `ui-conversation` (`EmptyHero.tsx`) | animated hero fish | `QizhiHeroEmblem` — glowing core with a slow orbit ring, plus the particle layer |
+
+The `official` build-profile gate is deliberately absent: this brand is not an
+overlay applied to a signed build, it is the deployment's own brand, so it
+occupies its slots whenever it is mounted.
+
+<a id="understand-the-implementation"></a>
+## Understand the implementation
+
+`src/index.ts` keeps an empty host `apply` so the Loader has a host-side row;
+all presentation ships through `exports["./client"]`. `src/client/index.ts`
+declares `inject = ['slots', 'theme']`, publishes the glass token layer, and
+registers the three occupants inside nested
+`ctx.slots.inject` calls, mirroring the official package's shape: each
+`register` returns a disposer, so unloading this plugin returns every slot to
+its shell fallback.
+
+`src/client/Brand.tsx` draws the mark as one `currentColor` SVG shape set, so
+the host's own label color keeps it legible at 24 px in the collapsed rail and
+at hero size. The wordmark is text, not an image: it localizes, stays
+selectable, and inherits the interface font.
+
+`src/client/ParticleField.tsx` is the only animated piece. One Canvas 2D context
+portalled to `document.body`: nodes drift at 11 px/s, wrap at the viewport edge,
+and stroke links inside 132 px. Budget scales with area
+(`width*height / 26_000`, clamped to 24–90 nodes), device-pixel ratio is capped
+at 2, the loop pauses on `document.hidden`, `prefers-reduced-motion` renders a
+single static frame, and resize re-seeds proportionally instead of restarting.
+The layer is `pointer-events: none` with `mix-blend-mode: screen`, so it adds
+glow on dark chrome without covering headline or composer text and cannot
+intercept a click.
+
+`src/client/glass.ts` carries the theme half, and it goes through the channel
+`ui-theme` reserves for third-party themes: `ctx.theme.overrideTokens(source,
+tokens)` stacks a partial alias layer over whichever base palette is active, and
+`ui-layout`'s presenter writes each value as an inline variable on `body`. That
+is why no stylesheet here fights the vendor sheet for specificity — inline
+tokens simply are the active palette. Every token ships a `{ light, dark }`
+pair, because a single value would go illegible the moment the user switches
+scheme. `src/styles/qizhi-theme.css` therefore keeps only what a token cannot
+express: the fixed ambient radial mesh behind `#root`, the document canvas
+colour, and the `backdrop-filter` that turns the now-translucent fills into
+frosted panels.
+
+The layer moves surface fills (`--dsw-alias-bg-base`,
+`--dsw-specific-sidebar-fill`, `--dsw-specific-input-major`, the three
+`bg-layer-*`, overlay, platform module, skeleton), the four `border-l*`
+hairlines — which `--dsw-elevation-stroke-color` follows, so elevated surfaces
+pick up the brand hairline without a hand-made shadow — and the brand/link and
+interactive hover accents. It never touches text tokens.
+
+Opacity is not uniform, and the reason is a real defect: only the two surfaces
+that sit directly on the ambient backdrop — the app canvas (`bg-base`) and the
+sidebar column — are see-through. Every token a panel, card or drawer paints
+*over app content* stays near-opaque (α ≥ 0.94), because a translucent fill
+there smears the transcript behind it. `tests/glass.spec.ts` pins that split so
+a future sweep cannot re-open it. Three upstream rules
+were treated as binding while choosing those: modal backdrops keep
+`--dsw-mask-blur: none` (no blur through a settings dialog), menu material
+(`--dsw-menu-surface-fill`, `--dsw-menu-backdrop-filter`) is not redefined and
+stays the shipped 40 px glass, and no surface pairs a `border-l*` outline with
+an elevation shadow.
+
+`buildGlassTokens(glass)` takes one capability flag: when the engine cannot
+composite a blur, or the OS asks for reduced transparency, the same keys are
+published with opaque values so a panel never shows other people's text through
+it.
+
+<a id="model-experience"></a>
+## Model Experience
+
+#### What the model sees
+
+Nothing. This package contributes browser presentation only: no prompt section,
+no tool schema, no session event, and no request field. The system prompt,
+tool list, and message history are byte-identical with it mounted or unmounted.
+
+#### KV-cache and token effect
+
+Zero. It changes no model-visible text, so it neither extends nor invalidates a
+cached request prefix.
+
+<a id="known-limitations-and-deferred-work"></a>
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+- **Copy that lives outside the slots is still edited in place.** The hero
+  headline and its subtitle are plain locale keys in `ui-conversation`
+  (`hero.headline`, `hero.subheading`) and the document title comes from
+  `brand.localBuild` in `packages/client/locale`; a brand package cannot reach
+  them, so those strings were changed at their source. A future brand slot for
+  the hero copy would let this package own them entirely.
+- **`ui-brand-official` stays installed but unmounted.** Keeping the dependency
+  row in `web-app/package.json` preserves the official build path; only the
+  composition changed.
+- **The frost needs a nameable surface, and CSS modules hide it.** Fill colours
+  reach every component through tokens, but `backdrop-filter` has no token, so
+  it is applied through selectors that survive hashing only by convention:
+  `aside` and the readable local-name suffix `_sidebarCol` — one surface, the
+  sidebar column, chosen because it is the only large element that paints its
+  own translucent fill. The list is short on purpose: blurring a *transparent*
+  layout wrapper (`nav`, `header`, `[class*='_panel']`, the composer seat)
+  frosts whatever content sits under it, which is how an earlier, broader
+  version of this rule ate half the page. An upstream rename drops the frost on
+  that surface; the fill and the layout are unaffected.
+- **Capability is read once, at activation.** `ctx.theme.overrideTokens` is a
+  stored layer, so a mid-session OS switch of `prefers-reduced-transparency`
+  does not re-pick opaque fills; a reload does. Engine blur support cannot
+  change within a session.
+- **Only one palette was observable live.** The running browser resolved
+  `system` to light, so the light path is measured in the DOM; the dark values
+  are pinned by `tests/glass.spec.ts` (every token carries both modes) rather
+  than by a screenshot.
+- **Chat-area chrome follows the palette, not a separate design.** Message
+  bubbles and tool cards inherit the rebinded `bg-layer-*` and hairlines; the
+  conversation typography is untouched.
+- **The orbit ring and particles are decorative** and hidden from the
+  accessibility tree, so assistive tech sees the same hero as before.
+- **Bilingual README pairing** is maintained by hand here; the repository's
+  `verify-translation-pairing` gate owns the canonical form.
